IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc22-pleas`

-- ccc22-tests-pleas.l4 -- tests for ccc22-pleas.l4 (sections 606 to 619). Expected values are written from the text, beside the assertion. Arguments are in the order of each function's GIVEN lines.

§ `Section 606`

-- (1): args: the accused is called on to plead, the plea.
#ASSERT `s 606(1) the accused may enter the plea` TRUE `s 606(1) guilty` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(1) the accused may enter the plea` TRUE `s 606(1) not guilty` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(1) the accused may enter the plea` TRUE `s 606(1) autrefois acquit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(1) the accused may enter the plea` TRUE `s 606(1) autrefois convict` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(1) the accused may enter the plea` TRUE `s 606(1) pardon` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(1) the accused may enter the plea` TRUE `s 606(1) an expungement order under the Expungement of Historically Unjust Convictions Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(1) the accused may enter the plea` TRUE `s 606(1) justification of a defamatory libel under section 611` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(1) the accused may enter the plea` TRUE `s 606(1) some other plea` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "and no others"
#ASSERT `s 606(1) the accused may enter the plea` FALSE `s 606(1) guilty` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not yet called on to plead
-- (1.1): args: voluntarily, understands (i) admission of the essential elements, (ii) nature and consequences, (iii) the court is not bound by any agreement, the facts support the charge.
#ASSERT `s 606(1.1) the court may accept a plea of guilty` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(1.1) the court may accept a plea of guilty` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 606(1.1) the court may accept a plea of guilty` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b)(i)
#ASSERT `s 606(1.1) the court may accept a plea of guilty` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b)(ii)
#ASSERT `s 606(1.1) the court may accept a plea of guilty` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b)(iii)
#ASSERT `s 606(1.1) the court may accept a plea of guilty` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 606(1.2) the court’s failure to inquire affects the validity of the plea` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "does not affect the validity of the plea"
#ASSERT `s 606(1.2) the court’s failure to inquire affects the validity of the plea` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): args: the accused refuses to plead, does not answer directly.
#ASSERT `s 606(2) the court must order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(2) the court must order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(2) the court must order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#TRACE `s 606(2) the court must order the clerk to enter a plea of not guilty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 606(2) order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty` AT 1
-- expected: FULFILLED
-- (3): arg: the accused asks for the trial to be postponed; the court considers that further time should be allowed.
#ASSERT `s 606(3) the accused is entitled as of right to have the trial postponed` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 606(3) the accused is entitled as of right to have the trial postponed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 606(3) the court may adjourn the trial to a later time in the session or sittings, or to the next of any subsequent session or sittings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(3) the court may adjourn the trial to a later time in the session or sittings, or to the next of any subsequent session or sittings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): args: pleads not guilty of the offence charged but guilty of another offence arising out of the same transaction, the prosecutor consents.
#ASSERT `s 606(4) the court may accept the plea of guilty of the other offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(4) the court may accept the plea of guilty of the other offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "with the consent of the prosecutor"
#ASSERT `s 606(4) the court may accept the plea of guilty of the other offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 606(4) the court must find the accused not guilty of the offence charged, find the accused guilty of the other offence and enter the findings in the record` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(4) the court must find the accused not guilty of the offence charged, find the accused guilty of the other offence and enter the findings in the record` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "if the plea is accepted"
-- (4.1): args: s 752 serious personal injury offence (a MAYBE), the offence is murder, the agreement, the court has accepted the plea.
#ASSERT `s 606(4.1) the court must inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the agreement` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a serious personal injury offence
#ASSERT `s 606(4.1) the court must inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the agreement` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- murder
#ASSERT `s 606(4.1) the court must inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the agreement` NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- murder, whatever section 752 answers
#ASSERT `s 606(4.1) the court must inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the agreement` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither
#ASSERT `s 606(4.1) the court must inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the agreement` NOTHING FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 752 does not decide
#ASSERT `s 606(4.1) the court must inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the agreement` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no agreement
#ASSERT `s 606(4.1) the court must inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the agreement` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the plea of guilty is not yet accepted: "after accepting the plea"
#TRACE `s 606(4.1) the court must inquire of the prosecutor after accepting the plea of guilty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 606(4.1) inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the agreement` AT 1
-- expected: FULFILLED
-- (4.2): the five-years helper. arg: the maximum imprisonment.
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more` `imprisonment for life` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- exactly five years
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 0, TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- five years less a day
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 4, 11, 0, FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 5, 1, 0, FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 6, 0, 0, TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- six years less a day is five years or more
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more` `no imprisonment is stated` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4.2): args: an offence as defined in section 2 of the Canadian Victims Bill of Rights, the class, the answer of the five-years function, the offence is referred to in (4.1), the agreement, the court has accepted the plea.
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the court must inquire of the prosecutor whether any of the victims had advised the prosecutor of their desire to be informed` TRUE `an indictable offence` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the court must inquire of the prosecutor whether any of the victims had advised the prosecutor of their desire to be informed` TRUE `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- FORK: a dual-procedure offence counted as "an indictable offence" (the text says it is "guilty of (a) an indictable offence")
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the court must inquire of the prosecutor whether any of the victims had advised the prosecutor of their desire to be informed` TRUE `an offence punishable on summary conviction` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the court must inquire of the prosecutor whether any of the victims had advised the prosecutor of their desire to be informed` FALSE `an indictable offence` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not an offence as defined in section 2 of the Canadian Victims Bill of Rights
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the court must inquire of the prosecutor whether any of the victims had advised the prosecutor of their desire to be informed` TRUE `an indictable offence` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- maximum below five years
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the court must inquire of the prosecutor whether any of the victims had advised the prosecutor of their desire to be informed` TRUE `an indictable offence` NOTHING FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the court must inquire of the prosecutor whether any of the victims had advised the prosecutor of their desire to be informed` TRUE `an indictable offence` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "that is not an offence referred to in subsection (4.1)"
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the court must inquire of the prosecutor whether any of the victims had advised the prosecutor of their desire to be informed` TRUE `an indictable offence` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no agreement
#ASSERT `s 606(4.2) the court must inquire of the prosecutor whether any of the victims had advised the prosecutor of their desire to be informed` TRUE `an indictable offence` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- plea not yet accepted
-- (4.3): args: (4.1) or (4.2) applies, the victim is dead or incapable, the victim was informed, s 2.2 answer for the individual (a MAYBE), that individual was informed.
#ASSERT `s 606(4.3) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victim of the agreement and the acceptance of the plea` TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 606(4.3) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victim of the agreement and the acceptance of the plea` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither (4.1) nor (4.2) applies
#ASSERT `s 606(4.3) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victim of the agreement and the acceptance of the plea` TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the victim was informed before the plea was accepted
#ASSERT `s 606(4.3) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victim of the agreement and the acceptance of the plea` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the victim is dead; the individual who may act on their behalf was informed
#ASSERT `s 606(4.3) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victim of the agreement and the acceptance of the plea` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the individual was not informed
#ASSERT `s 606(4.3) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victim of the agreement and the acceptance of the plea` TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 2.2 does not decide
#ASSERT `s 606(4.3) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victim of the agreement and the acceptance of the plea` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the person informed may not act for the victim, so the victim remains uninformed
#TRACE `s 606(4.3) the prosecutor must inform the victim as soon as feasible` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 606(4.3) take reasonable steps to inform the victim of the agreement and the acceptance of the plea` AT 5
-- expected: FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 606(4.4) the failure affects the validity of the plea` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 606(4.4) the failure affects the validity of the plea` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 606(4.4) the failure affects the validity of the plea` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 606(5) what the text shows` EQUALS "[Repealed, 2022, c. 17, s. 37]"

§ `Section 607`

#ASSERT `s 607(1) the accused may plead the special plea` `s 606(1) autrefois acquit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 607(1) the accused may plead the special plea` `s 606(1) autrefois convict` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 607(1) the accused may plead the special plea` `s 606(1) pardon` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 607(1) the accused may plead the special plea` `s 606(1) an expungement order under the Expungement of Historically Unjust Convictions Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 607(1) the accused may plead the special plea` `s 606(1) guilty` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 607(1) the accused may plead the special plea` `s 606(1) justification of a defamatory libel under section 611` EQUALS NOTHING   -- a special plea of another section
#ASSERT `s 607(2) the accused may plead in accordance with sections 611 and 612` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 607(2) the accused may plead in accordance with sections 611 and 612` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 607(3) the plea must be disposed of by the judge without a jury before the accused is called on to plead further` `s 606(1) pardon` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 607(3) the plea must be disposed of by the judge without a jury before the accused is called on to plead further` `s 606(1) autrefois acquit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 607(3) the plea must be disposed of by the judge without a jury before the accused is called on to plead further` `s 606(1) not guilty` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 607(4) the accused may plead guilty or not guilty` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 607(4) the accused may plead guilty or not guilty` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "When" the pleas are disposed of against the accused (ruling (b))
-- (5): args: pleads autrefois acquit or autrefois convict, states acquittal/conviction/discharge under 730(1), indicates time and place.
#ASSERT `s 607(5) the accused’s statement of the plea is sufficient` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 607(5) the accused’s statement of the plea is sufficient` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) missing
#ASSERT `s 607(5) the accused’s statement of the plea is sufficient` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) missing
#ASSERT `s 607(5) the accused’s statement of the plea is sufficient` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another plea
-- (6): args: the offence is one by virtue of subsections 7(2) to (3.1) or (3.7) or of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act, tried and convicted outside Canada, (a) not present and not represented, (b) not punished.
#ASSERT `s 607(6) the subsection bars the plea of autrefois convict` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 607(6) the subsection bars the plea of autrefois convict` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) fails: the person was punished
#ASSERT `s 607(6) the subsection bars the plea of autrefois convict` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) fails: present or represented
#ASSERT `s 607(6) the subsection bars the plea of autrefois convict` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 607(6) the subsection bars the plea of autrefois convict` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 608 to 609`

-- 608: args: an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict is tried, the material.
#ASSERT `s 608 the material is admissible in evidence to prove or to disprove the identity of the charges` TRUE `s 608 the evidence and adjudication on the former trial` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 608 the material is admissible in evidence to prove or to disprove the identity of the charges` TRUE `s 608 the notes of the judge and official stenographer on the former trial` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 608 the material is admissible in evidence to prove or to disprove the identity of the charges` TRUE `s 608 the record transmitted to the court under section 551 on the charge that is pending` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 608 the material is admissible in evidence to prove or to disprove the identity of the charges` TRUE `s 608 some other material` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 608 the material is admissible in evidence to prove or to disprove the identity of the charges` FALSE `s 608 the evidence and adjudication on the former trial` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 609(1): args: the issue is tried, (a) same matter, (b) might have been convicted of all the offences.
#ASSERT `s 609(1) the judge must give judgment discharging the accused in respect of the count` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 609(1) the judge must give judgment discharging the accused in respect of the count` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 609(1) the judge must give judgment discharging the accused in respect of the count` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 609(1) the judge must give judgment discharging the accused in respect of the count` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b)
-- 609(2): args: the issue is tried, it appears (a) / (b).
#ASSERT `s 609(2)(a) the judge must direct that the accused shall not be found guilty of any offence of which they might have been convicted on the former trial` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 609(2)(a) the judge must direct that the accused shall not be found guilty of any offence of which they might have been convicted on the former trial` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 609(2)(a) the judge must direct that the accused shall not be found guilty of any offence of which they might have been convicted on the former trial` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 609(2)(b) the accused must plead guilty or not guilty with respect to that offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 609(2)(b) the accused must plead guilty or not guilty with respect to that offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 609(2)(b) the accused must plead guilty or not guilty with respect to that offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 610`

-- (1): args: substantially the same offence as one previously convicted or acquitted, adds aggravation.
#ASSERT `s 610(1) the previous conviction or acquittal bars the subsequent indictment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 610(1) the previous conviction or acquittal bars the subsequent indictment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 610(1) the previous conviction or acquittal bars the subsequent indictment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): args: the previous indictment charged, the subsequent indictment charges, conviction or acquittal, same homicide.
#ASSERT `s 610(2) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter, infanticide or murder` `first degree murder` `manslaughter` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 610(2) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter, infanticide or murder` `second degree murder` `infanticide` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 610(2) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter, infanticide or murder` `manslaughter` `first degree murder` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 610(2) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter, infanticide or murder` `infanticide` `second degree murder` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 610(2) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter, infanticide or murder` `first degree murder` `second degree murder` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- that is subsection (3)
#ASSERT `s 610(2) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter, infanticide or murder` `manslaughter` `infanticide` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- that is subsection (4)
#ASSERT `s 610(2) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter, infanticide or murder` `first degree murder` `manslaughter` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 610(2) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter, infanticide or murder` `first degree murder` `manslaughter` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not the same homicide
#ASSERT `s 610(3) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as the other degree of murder` `first degree murder` `second degree murder` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 610(3) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as the other degree of murder` `second degree murder` `first degree murder` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 610(3) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as the other degree of murder` `first degree murder` `manslaughter` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 610(3) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as the other degree of murder` `first degree murder` `first degree murder` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 610(4) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter or infanticide` `infanticide` `manslaughter` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 610(4) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter or infanticide` `manslaughter` `infanticide` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 610(4) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter or infanticide` `manslaughter` `first degree murder` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 610(4) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter or infanticide` `manslaughter` `manslaughter` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 611 to 619`

-- 611(1): args: charged with publishing a defamatory libel, the plea is truth and public benefit.
#ASSERT `s 611(1) the accused may plead justification` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 611(1) the accused may plead justification` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 611(1) the accused may plead justification` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 611(2) the plea may justify the defamatory matter in that sense` TRUE `s 611(2) a sense in which the defamatory matter is specified in the count` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 611(2) the plea may justify the defamatory matter in that sense` TRUE `s 611(2) the sense that the defamatory matter bears without being specified` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 611(2) the plea may justify the defamatory matter in that sense` TRUE `s 611(2) separate pleas justifying the defamatory matter in each sense, pleaded separately to each count as if two libels had been charged in separate counts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 611(2) the plea may justify the defamatory matter in that sense` TRUE `s 611(2) some other sense` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 611(2) the plea may justify the defamatory matter in that sense` FALSE `s 611(2) a sense in which the defamatory matter is specified in the count` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 611(3): args: a plea under (1), in writing, sets out the particular facts.
#ASSERT `s 611(3) the plea is in the form subsection (3) requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 611(3) the plea is in the form subsection (3) requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 611(3) the plea is in the form subsection (3) requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 611(3) the plea is in the form subsection (3) requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 611(4) the prosecutor may in the reply deny generally the truth of the plea` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 611(4) the prosecutor may in the reply deny generally the truth of the plea` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 612(1): args: there is a plea of justification, charged with publishing the libel knowing it to be false.
#ASSERT `s 612(1) the section bars inquiring into the truth of the matters charged in the alleged libel` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 612(1) the section bars inquiring into the truth of the matters charged in the alleged libel` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "in the absence of a plea of justification"
#ASSERT `s 612(1) the section bars inquiring into the truth of the matters charged in the alleged libel` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless the accused is charged with publishing the libel knowing it to be false"
#ASSERT `s 612(1) the section bars inquiring into the truth of the matters charged in the alleged libel` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 612(1) evidence of the truth may be given to negative the allegation that the accused knew that the libel was false` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 612(1) evidence of the truth may be given to negative the allegation that the accused knew that the libel was false` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 612(2) the accused may also plead not guilty and the pleas are inquired into together` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 612(2) the accused may also plead not guilty and the pleas are inquired into together` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 612(3) the court may consider in pronouncing sentence whether the guilt of the accused is aggravated or mitigated by the plea` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 612(3) the court may consider in pronouncing sentence whether the guilt of the accused is aggravated or mitigated by the plea` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "and the accused is convicted"
#ASSERT `s 612(3) the court may consider in pronouncing sentence whether the guilt of the accused is aggravated or mitigated by the plea` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 613 the ground of defence may be relied on under the plea of not guilty` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- arg: a special plea is provided for the ground of defence
#ASSERT `s 613 the ground of defence may be relied on under the plea of not guilty` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 614 to 619 what the text shows` EQUALS "[ Repealed, 1991, c. 43, s. 3]"
